As of 12:16 p.m. ET, we are still missing your response.

Click here to take our one-minute Presidential survey  =E2=86=92

http://go.turnoutpac.org/Debate-Day-Survey

Tomorrow, Bernie, Hillary and O'Malley will take the stage for the final =
Democratic debate of 2015.

We're so proud to have Democratic leaders who debate substantive issues -- =
each of them has spoken out in favor of making it easier and simpler for =
Americans to vote.

All three Democrats are with us on boosting voter turnout. Now we need =
your help to finalize a winning strategy for Democrats on Election Day.=20

Take the PTP Debate Day Survey before tomorrow night at 8:00 p.m. ET =
=E2=86=92

http://go.turnoutpac.org/Debate-Day-Survey

Choose: Hillary Clinton, Bernie Sanders, Martin O'Malley, or undecided.

Voter turnout will be extra important in 2016 for two main reasons:

1) History proves that when Democrats get to the polls, Democrats win. But =
when Democrats don't vote, Republicans win big.

2) The Koch Brothers are copying the Obama playbook. They're paying for =
their own right-wing voter turnout machine, with teams of data engineers =
and operatives armed with iPads.

Koch-backed data engineers pore over their feedback in order to improve =
Republican strategy. If we're going to outsmart them, we need to hear from =
our best supporters.

Take the survey right now, before tomorrow night's debate, to develop our =
strategy for getting more Democrats to the polls in 2016:

http://go.turnoutpac.org/Debate-Day-Survey

Thanks for fighting with us,

-The Progressive Turnout Project


